# Architecture Rules — TypeScript

## Folder structure
Every feature lives in src/features/<featureName>/
  components/   — .tsx only
  hooks/        — useXxx.ts only
  actions/      — xxxActions.ts only
  services/     — xxxService.ts only
  types/        — xxx.types.ts (feature-specific types)

Shared reusable UI → src/components/
Shared hooks     → src/hooks/
Global types     → src/types/
Constants        → src/constants/

## Layer rules (never skip, never reverse)

### Component (.tsx)
- Returns JSX only
- Props must have an explicit interface: interface AuctionCardProps { ... }
- Calls hooks for data and callbacks
- NEVER imports a service or action directly
- NEVER contains useState/useEffect for data fetching
- NEVER uses `any` — type every prop

### Hook (useXxx.ts)
- Owns state: useState, useEffect, useReducer
- Calls action functions, not services
- Has explicit return type: const useAuctions = (): UseAuctionsReturn => {}
- Returns { data, isLoading, error, handlers }
- NEVER renders JSX
- NEVER imports a service directly
- One hook = one concern

### Action (xxxActions.ts)
- Plain async function, no React
- Has typed params and return: async function fetchAuctions(): Promise<Auction[]>
- Calls service functions, returns typed data or throws
- Contains business/transform logic
- NEVER imports useState/useEffect/any hook
- NEVER touches the DOM

### Service (xxxService.ts)
- HTTP calls only (fetch or axios)
- Returns typed raw response: Promise<ApiResponse<Auction[]>>
- No business logic, no state
- One file per API domain (auctionService, userService, walletService)

## TypeScript rules
- No `any` anywhere — use `unknown` and narrow it
- No type assertions (`as SomeType`) unless absolutely unavoidable
- All API response shapes must have an interface in xxx.types.ts
- Enums for fixed sets of values (AuctionStatus, BidStatus)
- Use type for unions, interface for object shapes
- All async functions must have explicit return types

## Code style rules
- No assumptions — receive data via props or hook, never derive from global
- Simple over clever — if a function is hard to name, split it
- No magic values — use typed constants (const MAX_BID = 1_000_000)
- No inline fetch inside components or hooks
- Reusable components must have zero feature-specific imports
- Export types alongside the file they belong to

## Data flow (one direction only)
Component → Hook → Action → Service → API
No skipping layers. No reverse imports.